"**Verdict: the CLI's error reporting is broken — it fails without signaling failure, and the OS return code cannot be trusted as a generation outcome.**\n\n## Setup\n\n`generate.py` located at `/mnt/skills/public/podcast-generation/scripts/generate.py` (384 lines, present and readable). Probe dir: `/mnt/user-data/outputs/podcast-cli-probe-w6bvlf8v`, containing a valid `script.json` (`{\"lines\":[{\"speaker\":\"male\",\"paragraph\":\"Hello\"}]}`) and a deliberately absent target `fresh-missing.mp3`.\n\nCredential check, by name only: none of `VOLCENGINE_TTS_APPID`, `VOLCENGINE_TTS_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `MINIMAX_API_KEY`, `PODCAST_GENERATION_PROVIDER` were set in my own environment to begin with, so the child env was clean by construction and also verified clean after the copy-and-pop. No values were read, printed, or logged at any point.\n\n## Case A — real invocation (`--script-file` + `--output-file`)\n\n- **returncode: 0**\n- **stdout:** `Error generating podcast: No credentials found. Set VOLCENGINE_TTS_APPID + VOLCENGINE_TTS_ACCESS_TOKEN for volcengine, or MINIMAX_API_KEY for minimax (optionally force with PODCAST_GENERATION_PROVIDER).`\n- **stderr:** `INFO:__main__:Loaded script with 1 lines`, then a full `Traceback`, ending in `ValueError: No credentials found...` raised from `_resolve_provider` via `_resolve_tts_provider` → `tts_node` → `generate_podcast`.\n- **MP3 exists: No** — size n/a. Only `script.json` is in the directory.\n\nThe failure is clean and early: provider resolution happens before any socket is opened, so no TTS network call was attempted, and no authorization header was ever constructed.\n\n## Case B — control, no arguments\n\n- **returncode: 2**\n- **stderr:** argparse usage line plus `generate.py: error: the following arguments are required: --script-file, --output-file`\n\nSo argument errors exit non-zero, but runtime failures exit zero.\n\n## The bug\n\nThe `__main__` block wraps the whole run in `try/except Exception`, prints the error, calls `traceback.print_exc()`, and then **falls off the end of the script** — there is no `sys.exit(1)` and no re-raise. Python's implicit exit status is 0. A caller doing `subprocess.run(...)` and checking `returncode == 0` will conclude the podcast was generated when nothing was written, and the only signal distinguishing success from failure is human-readable text on stdout/stderr.\n\nThat is precisely the trap the task warned about: return code 0 here means \"the interpreter finished,\" not \"audio exists.\" Generation outcome must be determined by filesystem evidence — the MP3 being present and non-zero in size. On that measure this run **failed**, as expected given no credentials.\n\nTwo secondary observations: the operational error message goes to stdout while the traceback goes to stderr, so a caller reading only stderr sees a traceback but no clean summary line; and the transcript file (if `--transcript-file` had been passed) would be written *before* TTS runs, so a failed generation can still leave a transcript behind — another reason not to infer success from side effects."